<!--
    Shared SpotBugs exclude filter for every Bloviate module.

    Every suppression below is scoped as narrowly as the finding allows and carries the
    reason it is safe. Blanket `<Match><Bug pattern="X"/></Match>` entries are avoided on
    purpose: a pattern suppressed everywhere hides the next genuine instance of it.

    Baseline this filter was written against (effort=Max, threshold=Medium):
      bloviate-core            26 findings
      bloviate-testcontainers   1 finding
      bloviate-junit            0 findings
      bloviate-datafaker        0 findings
    bloviate-benchmarks is not analysed at all (spotbugs.skip in its pom) — JMH's annotation
    processor generates ~10,200 UUF_UNUSED_FIELD findings in code no human maintains.
-->
<FindBugsFilter
        xmlns="https://github.com/spotbugs/filter/3.0.0"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="https://github.com/spotbugs/filter/3.0.0 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/spotbugs/spotbugs/master/spotbugs/etc/findbugsfilter.xsd">

    <!--
        Builder setters store the caller's reference instead of copying it.

        Bloviate's builders are construction-time scaffolding: a builder is populated and
        then consumed by build() on one thread, and the built object is what callers hold.
        Copying every List and java.util.Date on the way in would change documented aliasing
        semantics of the public builder API and add allocation to the generator construction
        path, which runs per column per fill.

        Scoped to nested Builder classes only, so the same pattern on a non-builder type is
        still reported.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Class name="~.*\$Builder$"/>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>

    <!--
        ColumnDefinition holds a DataGenerator: a collaborator the file writer invokes, not
        state to defend. Copying it is not possible (DataGenerator has no copy contract) and
        would be wrong if it were — the caller and the writer must share one generator instance
        so the value stream stays in sequence.

        ColumnConstraint used to be listed here too. Its canonical constructor now copies
        allowedValues, so the suppression is no longer needed for it.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Class name="io.bloviate.file.ColumnDefinition"/>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>

    <!--
        Constructors that validate their arguments and throw.

        Every flagged constructor is a Objects.requireNonNull / IllegalStateException guard.
        SpotBugs reports these because a partially-constructed object can be captured through
        a finalizer attack — which requires a subclass overriding finalize(). No class in this
        repository declares finalize(), and the flagged generator and filler constructors are
        private (instances come from their Builder), so no subclass can exist at all.

        Validating in the constructor is the correct design here; the alternative SpotBugs
        suggests (making the class final, or moving validation to a factory) would either
        break the builder pattern or move the check somewhere weaker.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Bug pattern="CT_CONSTRUCTOR_THROW"/>
    </Match>

</FindBugsFilter>
